# Light theme UI (single theme)

The app uses one theme: **editorial paperwork** (`html[data-theme="light"]`, cream paper, Inter + Roboto Mono, nekokata blue `#2A38B1`). Dark mode and `#themeToggleBtn` were removed.

## Non-negotiable

When changing **visible UI** (header, nav drawer, bottom bar, carousel, tiles, home stack, live island):

1. **Use CSS variables** from `www/styles/themes-light.css` and tokens, no hard-coded hex unless matching an existing pattern in the same component.
2. **Scope new styles** under `html[data-theme="light"]` or shared unscoped tokens in `www/styles/tokens.css`.
3. **Do not add** new `html[data-theme="dark"]` rules or reintroduce a theme toggle.

## Where styles live

| Area | Primary files |
|------|----------------|
| Tokens / shapes | `www/styles/tokens.css` |
| Shared primitives | `www/styles/primitives.css` |
| Theme colour bridges | `www/styles/themes-light.css` |
| **Shell chrome (header, drawer, bottom bar, carousel)** | `www/styles/shell-chrome.css` |
| **Glass material (chrome frost/blur/sheen)** | `www/styles/glass-material.css` |
| Tile language (category washes, tile radii) | `www/styles/tile-language.css` |
| Legacy inline CSS | `www/index.html` `<style>`, avoid new rules here, migrate to `www/styles/` |

Stylesheet order in `index.html`: tokens → brand → primitives → … → themes-light → glass-material → shell-chrome → tile-language.

## Contrast

Readable secondary text uses `--ui-text-dim` (bridged to `--ui-text-secondary`). Disabled/decorative only uses `--ui-text-disabled`, `--ui-border`, or `--mono-dim`.

## After `www/` edits

Run `npm run sync:android` before testing on device.
